### 4.1 Results from First Production

The results from the two production runs explained in Sec. 3.7 will be presented here. The two productions are different in terms of cut values and logic. An event can have several vertices. The first production used all vertices in a given event. However, we only need the best ranked (highest) vertex in a given event, therefore, the correlation between the rank of the event vertex to the multiplicity (gRefMult) can be used for an offline cut. The best vertices are the highest multiplicity ones. From Fig. 4.1, the cut gRefMult \(>50\) can be used to select the best vertex. This cut on gRefMult is included in all offline cut sets from first production unless otherwise specified. The first production used the cuts given in Table 3.5 and the pico cuts given in Table 3.7.

