cuts used are graphical selection cuts on: (1) decay length significance, (2) \(\rm DCA_{PV}^{D^{0}}\), and (3) decay length significance of daughter tracks \(K\) and \(\pi\). This plot was done using 26 million events.

This data set suffers from poor particle identification (PID) capability between kaon and pion for \(p_{T}>\) 0.7 \(\rm GeV/c\). One way to reduce the kaon-pion contamination is to impose a tighter cut on the \(N\sigma\). Another possibility is to use a momentum-dependent cut on the standard deviations of \(dE/dx\) distributions (\(N\sigma\)) cut. As shown in Fig. 4.19 we tried the PID cut based on the momentum region we used: For \(p_{T}<\) 1.2 \(\rm GeV/c\), we used the upper half of the kaon band (blue band) and lower half of the pion band (red band); 0 \(<\)\(|N\sigma_{K}|\) \(<\) 2 and -2 \(<\)\(|N\sigma_{\pi}|\)\(<\) 0. For \(p_{T}>\) 1.2 \(\rm GeV/c\), the cut was reversed, -2 \(<\)\(|N\sigma_{K}|\)\(<\) 0 and 0 \(<\)\(|N\sigma_{\pi}|\)\(<\) 2.

